<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the macOS build.

  Hardened runtime is required for notarization, and it also *denies* things the
  app needs by default, so each entry below is a deliberate widening:

    allow-jit                     Chromium's V8 compiles JavaScript at runtime. The
                                  renderer cannot start without it under the
                                  hardened runtime.
    allow-unsigned-executable-memory
                                  Part of the same JavaScript engine path; required
                                  by Electron's own documentation for hardened
                                  runtime builds.
    device.audio-input            The voice recorder uses getUserMedia({audio}).
                                  Without this the microphone prompt never appears
                                  and the feature is dead on macOS.

  Deliberately absent: camera, screen capture, location, address book, calendars,
  automation, and network client/server. The app needs none of them, and an
  entitlement is a claim the signed binary makes about itself.

  This is a threat-model change, not a copying exercise: see the A8 assumption in
  docs/THREAT-MODEL.md for what it widens and why it is accepted.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
